# =============================================================================
# Kanto .gitignore
# =============================================================================
#
# IMPORTANT — please read before removing entries from this file.
#
# Kanto is a multi-cloud system (OCI + Modal). The credential ignores below
# are intentional, defence-in-depth, and complement the gitleaks pre-commit
# and CI hooks. Any credential committed to public git history is compromised
# within hours, so we err on the side of over-ignoring credential-shaped
# files. If something legitimate is being ignored, prefer adding an explicit
# `!path/to/file` exception over loosening a pattern.
#
# Categories below, in order:
#   1. Python build artifacts and tooling caches
#   2. Virtual environments
#   3. IDE / editor files
#   4. OS junk
#   5. Local environment files (.env, .envrc) — but NOT *.example
#   6. Cloud credentials (OCI, Modal, GCP, AWS) and key material
#   7. Kubernetes config
#   8. Terraform state / plan / vars
#   9. Generic credential-shaped filenames at root and one level deep
#  10. Operator-local task spec files (kept out of repo)
#  11. Project-specific outputs (genome data, model weights)
#  12. Helm build artifacts (charts/*.tgz + Chart.lock under service charts)
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Python build artifacts and tooling caches
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt

.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.nox/

# uv lockfile — kept out of the repo per operator preference. Means CI
# resolves transitive deps fresh on every run; if a dependency cuts a
# breaking release we will discover it on the next CI run rather than
# at deploy time. Revisit if reproducibility issues bite.
uv.lock
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.cache
coverage.xml
*.cover
*.py,cover
.hypothesis/

# uv
.uv-cache/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Virtual environments
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.env-venv/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. IDE / editor files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.shared.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.project
.pydevproject
.settings/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
.cursor/
.aider*
CLAUDE.local.md

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. OS junk
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Local environment files
#     The .example variants ARE tracked; the real ones never are.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

.envrc
!.envrc.example

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Cloud credentials and key material
#     OCI, Modal, plus belt-and-braces for adjacent clouds in case operators
#     copy creds into the repo by accident while debugging.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OCI
.oci/
oci_api_key*.pem
oci_api_key*.pub
*_oci_*.pem
config.oci

# Modal — token file lives at ~/.modal.toml; never copy it into the repo.
.modal.toml
modal.toml
!modal.toml.example

# Generic key / cert material (any depth)
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.truststore
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
id_ecdsa
id_ecdsa.*
*_rsa
*_dsa
*_ed25519
*_ecdsa
known_hosts
authorized_keys

# Generic JSON-shaped credential blobs (at most two levels deep)
credentials.json
credentials.*.json
*-credentials.json
service-account*.json
gcp-*.json
aws-*.json
*/credentials.json
*/service-account*.json

# AWS / GCP — included so a misplaced cred from another env can't sneak in.
.aws/
.gcp/
gcloud/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. Kubernetes config — these embed cluster certs and bearer tokens.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
kubeconfig
kubeconfig.*
*.kubeconfig
.kube/
!.kube/.gitkeep

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. Terraform
#     *.tfvars frequently contain secrets in practice. The pre-commit hook
#     also blocks staging *.tfvars; this is the second line of defence.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!*.tfvars.example
!*.tfvars.json.example
infrastructure/terraform/config/*-backend.hcl
!infrastructure/terraform/config/*-backend.hcl.example

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 9. Generic credential-shaped filenames at root or one level deep
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
secret
secret.*
secrets
secrets.*
*_secret
*_secret.*
*-secret
*-secret.*
!*.example
/secret/
/secrets/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 10. Operator-local task spec files
#     Task descriptions for Tasks 0–17 are working documents the operator
#     hands to the implementer. They live alongside the repo for convenience
#     but are not part of the project history.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
task-*.md
PREREQUISITES_NOT_MET.md

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 11. Project-specific outputs
#     Large binary artifacts that should never live in git. The 1 MB
#     pre-commit hook also catches these, but explicit is better than
#     implicit.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.fna
*.fna.gz
*.faa
*.faa.gz
*.fasta
*.parquet
*.pt
*.pth
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.npz
data/
models/
!models/.gitkeep
weights/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 12. Helm build artifacts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `helm dependency update` writes both a Chart.lock and pulls each
# dependency into charts/*.tgz. Per infrastructure/helm/CONVENTIONS.md
# both are rebuilt in CI from Chart.yaml, so keep them out of the repo.
services/*/helm/charts/
services/*/helm/Chart.lock
